A||N||3||Eriamjh||Front Wheel Alignment questions.||||5||
Z||000000||Eriamjh||11-27-2001||07:18 AM||||OK, I'm rebuilding my '87's front end and I have a question about the "shims" and wheel alignment.<P>I know this suspension is not very adjustable.  When I took off the upper control arms, on one side there was a rather thick washer on both ends just inside of the bushing sleeves, but on the other side (drivers) both washers were on the rear side with nothing in front.<P>Should I duplicate this setup when I put it back together?<P>Just for reference, the old upper ball joints were installed with the flat side inward, which I think is what you do to adjust camber after some suspension wear.  I plan on putting the new ones in flat side out.<P>I'm sure the shop I take it to for an alignment is gonna hate me, but what else is there to do?<P>Any other tips for getting "close" on alignment before I take it to the shop?<P>------------------<BR>Dan||||reg||5
Z||000001||Oreif||11-27-2001||08:10 AM||||The small washers on the upper control arm is how they adjust caster. So you need to duplicate how they were when you took them off. As for upper ball joints, Get the MOOG adjustable ball joints. The bolt holes are slotted which makes it 1000 times easier to align the camber.<P>------------------<BR>            <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/LOGO3.jpg">          <BR><FONT SIZE="1"><B><I>Happiness isn't around the corner...<BR>Happiness IS the corner.</I></B></FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000002||Butter||11-27-2001||11:31 AM||||I would do what Oreif suggested.<P>Here is a link to a previous post I made that has the front and rear end info for an 84 model. <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum2/HTML/015432.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum2/HTML/015432.html</A> <P>||||reg||1
Z||000003||Eriamjh||11-27-2001||05:23 PM||||These Moog Problem solver BJs.  What is their model number?  Where can I get them?||||reg||1
